<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia5c6eb1705902dd8f87de701f4ee15fc3b389a3d" commit="19377425134c94f7c587e5b1ae20188171c3ba3f" commit_message="update_engine: Pass reboot description to powerd.  Make update_engine pass a description of why it's requesting a reboot to the Chrome OS power manager.  BUG=chromium:762328 TEST=built with FEATURES=test CQ-DEPEND=Ifcfcdde0df20e8e341e8aa9bc0002b10c56cd5e7  Change-Id: Ia5c6eb1705902dd8f87de701f4ee15fc3b389a3d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/658609 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="658609" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/system/update_engine" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/update_engine" ref="refs/changes/09/658609/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifcfcdde0df20e8e341e8aa9bc0002b10c56cd5e7" commit="26a396e2c0b3e5ca1f3cc279b3177f9117dcdc17" commit_message="power: Update Request{Restart,Shutdown} D-Bus signatures.  Update org.chromium.PowerManager.xml's signatures for powerd's RequestRestart and RequestShutdown D-Bus methods to include &quot;reason&quot; and &quot;description&quot; arguments. These are optional, but there's apparently no way to express that in a D-Bus XML file. I think. It's not like there are docs.  BUG=chromium:762328 TEST=built power_manager-client and packages that use it CQ-DEPEND=Ia5c6eb1705902dd8f87de701f4ee15fc3b389a3d CQ-DEPEND=CL:*451212  Change-Id: Ifcfcdde0df20e8e341e8aa9bc0002b10c56cd5e7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/658608 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="658608" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/08/658608/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2be8f242f56d803934fa8b27eebc5b98c41bd0bb" commit="fa677092a60322c76dbf5b8a4d15bd2768ac2e40" commit_message="cbuildbot: Fix issue with unibuild test suite exec  This forgiving case was originally in place to allow GoldenEye to launch the test plan feature.  Now that it's launched, it's no longer necessary, so default to an empty (fully filtered) array.  This will fix the attempts to still run test suites on hardware that is underprovisioned in the lab.  When reef-uni was deprovisioned last week, a couple DUTs were left, so it still attempted to schedule, which uncovered this issue.  Other DUTs had 0 provisioned, so Autotest reported an immediate pass due to insufficient DUTs.  BUG=b:65551979 TEST=./bin/cbuildbot_view_config --update and unit tests  Change-Id: I2be8f242f56d803934fa8b27eebc5b98c41bd0bb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/661377 Commit-Ready: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; Tested-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="661377" owner_email="shapiroc@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/77/661377/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I49030e6130f16b52e82391a4842e4700341acbe2" commit="5f3f4ad38d3ccb7495ea8bd9cedb2ae36aabc811" commit_message="media-libs/arc-mesa: Rename gallium_driver_enable  Rename gallium_driver_enable to gallium_enable, which is the name used in the upstream ebuild. According to my inspection of upstream's git log, it was always named gallium_enable.  BUG=b:36895696 TEST=emerge-reef arc-mesa  Change-Id: I49030e6130f16b52e82391a4842e4700341acbe2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/660381 Commit-Ready: Chad Versace &lt;chadversary@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chad Versace &lt;chadversary@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="660381" owner_email="chadversary@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/81/660381/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I061a943a21b99fdd174ed4d3f3136fc07d34b4a3" commit="3ecae6d413871c7af281561b50d1d24cbc48a46f" commit_message="Refactor Buildbucket for GAE Apps.  BUG=chromium:746514 TEST=unit_tests  Change-Id: I061a943a21b99fdd174ed4d3f3136fc07d34b4a3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/630356 Commit-Ready: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="630356" owner_email="nxia@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/56/630356/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3ea8bb5ba3f19f0ba5bb863ee4d67b7bf3fbc939" commit="fea1e0d96b3abb1f7c876112c0e67175bca937b7" commit_message="p2p_ShareFiles: Fix file write race condition.  Somewhere at the end of this test, a 10 byte files is created and assumed the p2p-server shares the file (with correct size) back to the simulator. But on some boards this may flake when the p2p-server shares the file info before its content is written to disk. This causes the test fail because the expected file on the DUT was not found.  This patch wraps the call to get_peer_files() in another function to check for the correctness of the file name and size before complaining. However, if the file is never shared (due to some unknown problem), the simulator does not raise an exception on timeout. This additional problem is outside the scope of this bug.  BUG=chromium:762579 TEST=test_that --board=nyan_kitty chromeos4-row13-rack1-host3.cros p2p_ShareFiles  Change-Id: I3ea8bb5ba3f19f0ba5bb863ee4d67b7bf3fbc939 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/660783 Commit-Ready: Amin Hassani &lt;ahassani@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Amin Hassani &lt;ahassani@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="660783" owner_email="ahassani@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/83/660783/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7bb195861ed2c60598cf8646912b61580fb24b25" commit="c91996fe93b1f2c293facd4a1a53f53e3887c7bb" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Fix TK configuration to the driver in EAPOL-Key 3/4 retry case  Commit 7d711541dced759b34313477d5d163e65c5b0131 ('Clear TK part of PTK after driver key configuration') started clearing TK from memory immediately after having configured it to the driver when processing EAPOL-Key message 3/4. While this covered the most common case, it did not take into account the possibility of the authenticator having to retry EAPOL-Key message 3/4 in case the first EAPOL-Key message 4/4 response is lost. That case ended up trying to reinstall the same TK to the driver, but the key was not available anymore.  Fix the EAPOL-Key message 3/4 retry case by configuring TK to the driver only once. There was no need to try to set the same key after each EAPOL-Key message 3/4 since TK could not change. If actual PTK rekeying is used, the new TK will be configured once when processing the new EAPOL-Key message 3/4 for the first time.  (backported from hostap commit ad00d64e7d8827b3cebd665a0ceb08adabf15e1e)  BUG=chromium:762671 TEST=wifi_matfunc  Change-Id: I7bb195861ed2c60598cf8646912b61580fb24b25 Signed-off-by: Jouni Malinen &lt;jouni@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/657895 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="657895" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/hostap" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hostap" ref="refs/changes/95/657895/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I13f7e446550701d5191f2c4bb0737fc19d4e1c31" commit="23af4af8e9073bba0c485838f4bd94274ac3442f" commit_message="libcontainer: Include limits.h, needed for PATH_MAX  This was failing to build with:  [1/2] CC obj/libcontainer/libcontainer.libcontainer.o FAILED: obj/libcontainer/libcontainer.libcontainer.o armv7a-cros-linux-gnueabi-clang -MMD -MF obj/libcontainer/libcontainer.libcontainer.o.d -DUSE_device_mapper=0 -D_LARGEFILE_SOURCE -D_LARGEFILE64_SOURCE -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 -I../../../../.. /../../../../mnt/host/source/src/platform2/libcontainer -Iobj/libcontainer/libcontainer.gen/include -Igen/include -I/mnt/host/source/src/platform2 -I/mnt/host/source/src/platform -I/build/loo nix/usr/include -Wall -Wno-psabi -Wunused -Wno-unused-parameter -ggdb3 -fstack-protector-strong -Wformat=2 -fvisibility=internal -Wa,--noexecstack -Werror --sysroot=/build/loonix -fvisibility =default -I/build/loonix/usr/include/chromeos -fPIC -std=gnu11 -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 -D_LARGEFILE_SOURCE -D_LARGEFILE64_SOURCE -O2 -O2 -pipe -march=armv7-a -mtune=cortex-a9 -mfpu=neon -mfloa t-abi=hard -g -fno-exceptions -fno-unwind-tables -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables -clang-syntax -clang-